window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Dylan St. James is The Fatal Five's most prized possession. The leader's little sister and the most untouchable girl at Stonedge University. She’s the girl all the boys want but can’t have and the girls love to hate. That is, until one night, one race, and everything changed.</p> <p>Drugged. Beaten. Raped.</p> <p>They thought they were smart. They thought she wouldn’t remember, but the men who hurt her also walk the same grounds that she does. Day after day, they spew taunts and threats. Thinking they would get away with it. But little did they know, she’s a killer too, and she’s out for revenge. But she can’t do it alone so she tells the only person she trusts.</p> <p>Easton Daniels. Her brother's best friend. The most lethal of The Fatal Five.</p> <p>They really thought they could get away with what they did. But they were mistaken. They might have had the jump on me, but nothing could prepare them for what’s to come. They have no idea that touching what didn’t belong to them would cost them their life. She is mine. A part of me, which makes her part of us. The Fatal Five are one. And messing with any of us will have an outcome just as it sounds; Fatal.</p> <p>What would you do if the one person you trusted the most was hidden in plain sight? Lying to you day in and day out, leaving you with the remnants of the guilty? And once everything implodes, how do you forgive and forget?</p> <p>Remnants Of The Guilty: The Fatal Five is a MF Dark, Brother’s Best Friend, College-Aged Romance. This does not end with a cliffhanger and is a part of an interconnected standalone series. This book is intended for listeners 18 years and older. Please check the author’s website for a full list of content warnings.</p>"; 
